    <div class="itdgl-evidence-band">
      <strong>ITD CLINIC MARKETING &mdash; WHAT WE ACTUALLY DO:</strong>
      ITD GrowthLabs runs full-stack digital marketing for dermatology + skincare clinics across Thane, Mumbai, Navi Mumbai, Dombivli, Kalyan, Nagpur, Nashik, and Pune. Social media management + Reels + viral content, Meta + Google ads, website + online booking + WhatsApp Cloud API integration, Google Business Profile optimisation + local SEO, and patient lead generation. We work with clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams — treating the marketing function as an outsourced growth partner, not a vendor. Every answer below reflects live clinic work.
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What channel mix for Meta + Google ads for a Nashik dermatology clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Typical allocation: Meta (Facebook + Instagram + Reels + WhatsApp CTWA) 40-50%, Google Search + Ads 20-25%, Google Shopping (Local Services Ads for booked-consultation) 5-10%, Google Business Profile local ads 10-15%, YouTube ads (Reels + long-form retargeting) 5-10%, WhatsApp CTWA (click-to-WhatsApp) 5-10%. In Nashik with Marathi + emerging tourism + wine industry + agricultural wealth + salaried + growing middle class + Kumbh-tourism-adjacent, Meta Instagram + Reels dominant due to visual + creator-driven skincare discovery.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What CPL should we expect for dermatology ads in Nashik?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In Nashik: Rs 150-500 for general consultation inquiry, Rs 300-800 for specific-procedure inquiry (HydraFacial + laser + Botox), Rs 500-1,200 for high-AOV procedure (acne treatment package + full facial rejuvenation). Lead-to-booked-consultation conversion 20-40% (higher with WhatsApp handoff). Cost per booked consultation: Rs 400-2,500. Consultation-to-treatment conversion 30-60%. Effective cost per acquired patient: Rs 1,500-8,000 for Nashik dermatology clinic well-optimised.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic monthly ad budget for a Nashik dermatology clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Rs 30,000-2.8 lakh. Starter (Rs 30-80K/month Nashik) suits solo clinic Rs 3-8 lakh/month revenue. Growth (Rs 80K-2.5L Nashik) for 2-3 doctor Rs 8-40 lakh/month. Enterprise (Rs 2.5-6L Nashik) for multi-location Rs 40 lakh+/month. Rule: 15-25% of monthly clinic revenue during acquisition-focused growth phase, 8-15% during retention-optimised mature phase.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What creative formats work best for dermatology paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Meta + Instagram + Reels: (1) Compliance-safe before-after carousel + Reels (highest engagement), (2) Condition + procedure educational video, (3) Doctor-testimonial video with credentials, (4) Patient testimonial video with signed consent, (5) Facility + team + BTS content, (6) Limited-time consultation-booking offer with clear CTA. Google Search: text + sitelinks + call extension + location extension + review snippets. YouTube: 15-30s Reels + 6s bumper + 30-90s long-form for retargeting.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What compliance rules apply to dermatology paid ads in Nashik?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">ASCI medical advertising code + Maharashtra Medical Council + Meta + Google medical-vertical policies. Compliant approach: (1) education-first ad copy (no guaranteed outcome), (2) before-after with patient consent + disclaimer, (3) no comparative claims, (4) no prescription-drug promotion, (5) no aggressive discounting on medical decisions, (6) Meta + Google restrict some medical categories (dermatology mostly allowed with proper claim language). In Nashik, Maharashtra Medical Council + Maharashtra FDA + NMC (Nashik Municipal Corporation) enforcement.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does Meta CAPI + Google Enhanced Conversions setup work for a Nashik dermatology clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Server-side event tracking essential — recovers 15-30% attribution lost to iOS 14+ tracking restrictions. Meta CAPI via Shopify/WordPress plugin OR direct API integration. Google Enhanced Conversions via GA4 + Google Tag Manager server-side. WhatsApp CTWA click tracking + revenue attribution. Weekly attribution audit + monthly cohort review + first-purchase vs LTV comparison. In Nashik, WhatsApp-heavy purchase path requires CTWA + custom UTM structure.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we handle attribution + LTV/CAC for dermatology paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">CRM (Zoho/HubSpot/native clinic-management-system) with source-channel tracking → lead scoring → consultation booking → treatment conversion → cohort LTV. UTM discipline on every ad + landing page + WhatsApp handoff. LTV/CAC dashboard weekly. Value-based bidding (LTV-weighted vs first-consultation CPA). Dermatology 24-month LTV typical Rs 25,000-3 lakh (concern-specific plan + repeat + upsell). Payback 2-6 months.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we control ad fatigue for dermatology paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Creative velocity: 8-15 units/week Growth-tier. Below velocity, CPL climbs 25-50% within 60 days. Audience expansion + lookalike refresh 2-4 weeks. Creative refresh 3-4 weeks. Frequency capping 3-5/week per audience. Exclude converted patients from prospecting. Creator UGC injection into retargeting. Seasonal + peak-window campaigns disrupt fatigue naturally (Diwali + wedding season + Winter + Kumbh Mela cycle + Ganesh Chaturthi + wine harvest season).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are common paid-ads mistakes for Nashik dermatology clinics?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Optimising for first-consultation CPA vs LTV (compresses long-term margin). (2) Low creative velocity. (3) No Meta CAPI (30% attribution loss). (4) Weak landing pages (bad LP kills paid conversion). (5) No WhatsApp CTWA handoff (leads leak). (6) ASCI-violating ad copy. (7) English-only creative in Nashik. (8) Same audience + creative for all procedures (should segment). (9) No creator UGC in retargeting. (10) Ignoring peak-season concentration (Diwali + wedding season + Winter + Kumbh Mela cycle + Ganesh Chaturthi + wine harvest season).</div>
      </div>
